        "content": "# Technical Design: YAML Validator CLI Command\n\n**Feature ID**: add a simple yaml validator command without adding new deps\n**Version**: 1.0.0\n**Status**: Draft\n**Created**: 2026-02-20\n\n---\n\n## 1. Design Overview\n\nThis feature adds a `bun run validate` CLI command that accepts a single YAML file path, parses it using a custom lightweight YAML syntax validator written in TypeScript, and reports whether the file is syntactically valid or contains errors. The entire implementation lives within the project with zero new production dependencies. A custom YAML parser module provides the validation logic, and a CLI entry point script handles argument parsing, file I/O, output formatting, and exit codes.\n\n### High-Level Architecture\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    A[\"Developer Terminal\"] -->|\"bun run validate file.yaml\"| B[\"validate-yaml.ts<br/>(CLI Entry Point)\"]\n    B -->|\"reads file\"| C[\"Filesystem<br/>(Bun.file API)\"]\n    B -->|\"passes content\"| D[\"yaml-parser.ts<br/>(Validation Engine)\"]\n    D -->|\"YamlValidationResult\"| B\n    B -->|\"stdout / stderr\"| A\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Architecture\n\n### 2.1 Component Diagram\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TB\n    subgraph \"package.json scripts\"\n        S[\"validate script\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"src/\"\n        CLI[\"validate-yaml.ts<br/>CLI Entry Point\"]\n        PARSER[\"yaml-parser.ts<br/>YAML Validation Engine\"]\n        UTILS[\"utils.ts<br/>(existing, unchanged)\"]\n        INDEX[\"index.ts<br/>(existing, unchanged)\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Runtime APIs\"\n        ARGV[\"process.argv\"]\n        EXIT[\"process.exit\"]\n        STDOUT[\"process.stdout\"]\n        STDERR[\"process.stderr\"]\n        BUNFILE[\"Bun.file()\"]\n    end\n\n    S -->|\"bun run\"| CLI\n    CLI --> ARGV\n    CLI --> EXIT\n    CLI --> STDOUT\n    CLI --> STDERR\n    CLI --> BUNFILE\n    CLI -->|\"import validateYaml\"| PARSER\n```\n\n### 2.2 Sequence Diagram -- Valid File\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant Dev as Developer\n    participant CLI as validate-yaml.ts\n    participant FS as Filesystem (Bun.file)\n    participant Parser as yaml-parser.ts\n\n    Dev->>CLI: bun run validate config.yaml\n    CLI->>CLI: Read process.argv[2]\n    CLI->>FS: Bun.file(filePath)\n    FS-->>CLI: File handle\n    CLI->>FS: file.exists() / file.text()\n    FS-->>CLI: file content (string)\n    CLI->>Parser: validateYaml(content)\n    Parser-->>CLI: { valid: true }\n    CLI->>Dev: stdout: \"Valid YAML: config.yaml\"\n    CLI->>CLI: process.exit(0)\n```\n\n### 2.3 Sequence Diagram -- Invalid File\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant Dev as Developer\n    participant CLI as validate-yaml.ts\n    participant FS as Filesystem (Bun.file)\n    participant Parser as yaml-parser.ts\n\n    Dev->>CLI: bun run validate broken.yaml\n    CLI->>CLI: Read process.argv[2]\n    CLI->>FS: Bun.file(filePath)\n    FS-->>CLI: File handle\n    CLI->>FS: file.exists() / file.text()\n    FS-->>CLI: file content (string)\n    CLI->>Parser: validateYaml(content)\n    Parser-->>CLI: { valid: false, error: { message, line } }\n    CLI->>Dev: stderr: \"Invalid YAML: broken.yaml\\n  Error on line 12: ...\"\n    CLI->>CLI: process.exit(1)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Detailed Design\n\n### 3.1 Data Model\n\nThe parser exposes a single result type used as its return contract:\n\n```typescript\n/**\n * Result of YAML syntax validation.\n */\nexport interface YamlValidationResult {\n  /** Whether the YAML content is syntactically valid. */\n  valid: boolean;\n  /** Error details, present only when valid is false. */\n  error?: {\n    /** Human-readable description of the syntax problem. */\n    message: string;\n    /** 1-based line number where the error was detected. */\n    line: number;\n    /** 1-based column number where the error was detected (when available). */\n    column?: number;\n  };\n}\n```\n\n### 3.2 Module: `src/yaml-parser.ts` -- YAML Validation Engine\n\n**Purpose**: Accepts a YAML content string and returns a `YamlValidationResult` indicating syntactic validity.\n\n**Public API**:\n\n```typescript\nexport function validateYaml(content: string): YamlValidationResult;\n```\n\n**Internal Design -- Line-by-Line State Machine**:\n\nThe parser processes the input line by line, maintaining the following state:\n\n| State Field | Type | Purpose |\n|-------------|------|---------|\n| `indentStack` | `number[]` | Stack of indentation levels for nested blocks |\n| `inMultiLineScalar` | `boolean` | Whether currently inside a multi-line scalar (`\\|` or `>`) |\n| `multiLineIndent` | `number` | Expected minimum indent for multi-line scalar content |\n| `flowDepth` | `number` | Nesting depth of flow collections `{}` / `[]` |\n| `lineNumber` | `number` | Current 1-based line number |\n\n**Validation Checks Performed (per line)**:\n\n| Check | Description | Error Produced |\n|-------|-------------|----------------|\n| Tab detection | Lines using tab characters for indentation | \"Tab characters are not allowed for indentation in YAML\" |\n| Indentation consistency | Indentation must be consistent within a block context (spaces only, monotonically managed) | \"Invalid indentation: expected N spaces, found M\" |\n| Quote balancing | Single-quoted and double-quoted strings must be properly closed within the line (accounting for escaped quotes in double-quoted strings) | \"Unterminated quoted string\" |\n| Mapping syntax | Mapping entries must follow `key: value` or `key:` with valid key characters | \"Invalid mapping syntax\" |\n| Flow collection balancing | `{` / `}` and `[` / `]` must be properly nested and balanced across lines | \"Unclosed flow collection\" or \"Unexpected closing bracket\" |\n| Document markers | `---` and `...` are valid only at column 0 with no leading whitespace | Validated as special lines |\n| Multi-line scalar indicators | `\\|`, `>`, `\\|+`, `\\|-`, `>+`, `>-` following a mapping key trigger multi-line mode | Tracked for subsequent lines |\n| Comment handling | `#` preceded by whitespace or at line start is a comment | Lines/tails after comment marker are ignored |\n| Directive handling | `%YAML` and `%TAG` directives at document start | Recognized and skipped |\n\n**YAML Features Covered (basic subset)**:\n\n- Block mappings (`key: value`, nested)\n- Block sequences (`- item`, nested)\n- Scalar values (plain, single-quoted, double-quoted)\n- Comments (`# comment`)\n- Multi-line scalars (literal `|` and folded `>` with chomping modifiers)\n- Flow collections (`{key: value}`, `[item1, item2]`)\n- Document markers (`---`, `...`)\n- Empty documents (valid per spec)\n- Blank lines\n- Anchors (`&name`) and aliases (`*name`) -- recognized syntactically\n\n**YAML Features NOT Covered (out of scope per requirements)**:\n\n- Custom tags (`!tag`)\n- Complex keys (multi-line keys, `? key`)\n- Merge keys (`<<:`)\n- Full Unicode validation beyond what TypeScript/Bun handles\n- Byte order mark handling\n- Full YAML 1.2 spec edge cases\n\n### 3.3 Module: `src/validate-yaml.ts` -- CLI Entry Point\n\n**Purpose**: Serves as the script invoked by `bun run validate`. Handles argument parsing, file I/O, output formatting, and process exit codes.\n\n**Flow**:\n\n```\n1. Read filePath from process.argv[2]\n2. If no filePath -> print usage to stderr, exit(1)\n3. Resolve filePath (handle relative/absolute)\n4. Check file existence via Bun.file(filePath).exists()\n5. If not exists -> print \"Error: File not found - {filePath}\" to stderr, exit(1)\n6. Read file content via Bun.file(filePath).text()\n7. If read fails (permissions, directory) -> print \"Error: Cannot read file - {filePath}\" to stderr, exit(1)\n8. Call validateYaml(content)\n9. If valid -> print \"Valid YAML: {filePath}\" to stdout, exit(0)\n10. If invalid -> print error to stderr, exit(1)\n```\n\n**Output Formats**:\n\n| Scenario | Stream | Format | Exit Code |\n|----------|--------|--------|-----------|\n| Valid YAML | stdout | `Valid YAML: {filePath}` | 0 |\n| Invalid YAML | stderr | `Invalid YAML: {filePath}\\n  Error on line {N}: {message}` | 1 |\n| Invalid YAML (with column) | stderr | `Invalid YAML: {filePath}\\n  Error on line {N}, column {C}: {message}` | 1 |\n| File not found | stderr | `Error: File not found - {filePath}` | 1 |\n| Cannot read file | stderr | `Error: Cannot read file - {filePath}` | 1 |\n| No arguments | stderr | `Usage: bun run validate <file.yaml>` | 1 |\n\n**Security**:\n\n- File is opened read-only via `Bun.file().text()` (no write operations)\n- No `eval()` or dynamic code execution on file content\n- Only the single explicitly-provided path is accessed\n\n### 3.4 Integration: `package.json`\n\nAdd a single new script entry:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"validate\": \"bun run src/validate-yaml.ts\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nInvocation: `bun run validate path/to/file.yaml`\n\nArguments after the script name are forwarded to the underlying script by Bun, so `process.argv[2]` receives the file path.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Technology Stack\n\n| Layer | Technology | Rationale |\n|-------|-----------|-----------|\n| Runtime | Bun | Existing project runtime |\n| Language | TypeScript (strict mode) | Existing project language |\n| File I/O | `Bun.file()` API | Bun-native, async-capable, already available |\n| CLI Args | `process.argv` | Standard Node/Bun API, no library needed |\n| Output | `console.log` / `console.error` | Maps to stdout/stderr respectively |\n| Exit Codes | `process.exit()` | Standard process API |\n| Testing | `bun:test` | Existing project test framework |\n| YAML Parsing | Custom `src/yaml-parser.ts` | Zero-dependency constraint (FR-007); user-confirmed decision |\n\n**New production dependencies**: None\n**New dev dependencies**: None\n\n---\n\n## 5. Implementation Plan\n\n### T1: YAML Validation Engine (`src/yaml-parser.ts`)\n\nCreate the core YAML syntax validation module.\n\n- Define and export `YamlValidationResult` interface\n- Implement and export `validateYaml(content: string): YamlValidationResult` function\n- Implement internal line-by-line state machine:\n  - Indentation tracking and validation\n  - Quote balancing (single and double, with escape handling)\n  - Flow collection nesting (`{}`, `[]`)\n  - Multi-line scalar detection and tracking (`|`, `>`)\n  - Comment stripping\n  - Document marker recognition (`---`, `...`)\n  - Mapping and sequence entry validation\n  - Tab character detection in indentation\n- Handle edge cases: empty input, whitespace-only input, comment-only input\n- Estimated size: 200-400 lines\n\n### T2: CLI Entry Point (`src/validate-yaml.ts`)\n\nCreate the CLI command script.\n\n- Parse `process.argv[2]` for file path argument\n- Implement usage message when no argument provided\n- Implement file existence check via `Bun.file().exists()`\n- Implement file reading via `Bun.file().text()` with try/catch\n- Call `validateYaml()` with file content\n- Format and print output (success to stdout, errors to stderr)\n- Set exit codes via `process.exit()`\n- Estimated size: 50-80 lines\n\n### T3: Parser Unit Tests (`src/yaml-parser.test.ts`)\n\nCreate comprehensive tests for the YAML validation engine.\n\n- Valid YAML test cases:\n  - Simple key-value mapping\n  - Nested mappings\n  - Sequences (lists)\n  - Mixed mappings and sequences\n  - Comments (full-line and inline)\n  - Empty document\n  - Whitespace-only document\n  - Comment-only document\n  - Multi-line scalars (literal and folded)\n  - Flow collections\n  - Document markers\n  - Quoted strings (single and double)\n  - Anchors and aliases\n- Invalid YAML test cases:\n  - Tab indentation\n  - Inconsistent indentation\n  - Unterminated quoted strings\n  - Unclosed flow collections\n  - Unexpected closing brackets\n  - Malformed mapping syntax\n- Verify error objects include correct line numbers\n- Estimated: 30-50 test cases\n\n### T4: CLI Integration Tests (`src/validate-yaml.test.ts`)\n\nCreate tests for the CLI command behavior using `Bun.spawn`