        "content": "# Development Tasks: YAML Validator CLI Command\n\n**Feature ID**: add a simple yaml validator command without adding new deps\n**Status**: Not Started\n**Progress**: 0% (0 of 7 tasks)\n**Estimated Effort**: 3 days\n**Started**: 2026-02-20\n\n## Overview\n\nAdd a `bun run validate` CLI command that accepts a single YAML file path, parses it using a custom lightweight YAML syntax validator written in TypeScript, and reports whether the file is syntactically valid or contains errors. Zero new production dependencies. A custom YAML parser module provides the validation logic, and a CLI entry point script handles argument parsing, file I/O, output formatting, and exit codes.\n\n## Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. **[T1]** - Core parser module; no dependencies on other new components\n2. **[T2, T3]** - CLI entry point imports T1's interface; parser tests import T1's exports. Both depend only on T1 and are independent of each other.\n3. **[T4, T5]** - CLI tests invoke T2; package.json references T2. Both depend only on T2 and are independent of each other.\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T2 -> T1 (Interface dependency: CLI imports `validateYaml` and `YamlValidationResult` from parser module)\n- T3 -> T1 (Interface dependency: tests import `validateYaml` to assert behavior)\n- T4 -> T2 (Build dependency: integration tests spawn the CLI script)\n- T5 -> T2 (Build dependency: script entry references the CLI file)\n\n**Critical Path**: T1 -> T2 -> T4\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Foundation\n\n- [ ] **T1**: Create the YAML validation engine (`src/yaml-parser.ts`) with a line-by-line state machine parser `[complexity:complex]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#32-module-srcyaml-parserts--yaml-validation-engine](design.md#32-module-srcyaml-parserts--yaml-validation-engine)\n\n    **Effort**: 8 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] File `src/yaml-parser.ts` exists and exports the `YamlValidationResult` interface with `valid: boolean` and optional `error: { message: string; line: number; column?: number }`\n    - [ ] File exports a `validateYaml(content: string): YamlValidationResult` function\n    - [ ] Parser implements a line-by-line state machine tracking `indentStack`, `inMultiLineScalar`, `multiLineIndent`, `flowDepth`, and `lineNumber`\n    - [ ] Detects tab characters used for indentation and returns an error with the correct line number\n    - [ ] Validates indentation consistency within block contexts (spaces only, monotonically managed via indent stack)\n    - [ ] Detects unterminated single-quoted and double-quoted strings (accounting for escaped quotes in double-quoted strings)\n    - [ ] Tracks and validates flow collection nesting (`{}` and `[]`) and reports unclosed or unexpected closing brackets\n    - [ ] Recognizes and validates document markers (`---` and `...`) at column 0\n    - [ ] Detects and tracks multi-line scalar indicators (`|`, `>`, `|+`, `|-`, `>+`, `>-`) following a mapping key\n    - [ ] Strips comments (`#` preceded by whitespace or at line start) before performing other checks\n    - [ ] Recognizes `%YAML` and `%TAG` directives and skips them\n    - [ ] Handles edge cases: empty input returns `{ valid: true }`, whitespace-only input returns `{ valid: true }`, comment-only input returns `{ valid: true }`\n    - [ ] Recognizes anchors (`&name`) and aliases (`*name`) syntactically\n    - [ ] Validates block mapping entries (`key: value`, `key:`) and block sequence entries (`- item`)\n\n### CLI and Parser Tests\n\n- [ ] **T2**: Create the CLI entry point script (`src/validate-yaml.ts`) that handles argument parsing, file I/O, output formatting, and exit codes `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#33-module-srcvalidate-yamlts--cli-entry-point](design.md#33-module-srcvalidate-yamlts--cli-entry-point)\n\n    **Effort**: 4 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] File `src/validate-yaml.ts` exists and imports `validateYaml` from `./yaml-parser`\n    - [ ] Reads file path from `process.argv[2]`\n    - [ ] When no argument is provided, prints `Usage: bun run validate <file.yaml>` to stderr and exits with code 1\n    - [ ] Resolves the file path and checks existence via `Bun.file(filePath).exists()`\n    - [ ] When file does not exist, prints `Error: File not found - {filePath}` to stderr and exits with code 1\n    - [ ] Reads file content via `Bun.file(filePath).text()` wrapped in try/catch\n    - [ ] When file cannot be read (permissions, directory), prints `Error: Cannot read file - {filePath}` to stderr and exits with code 1\n    - [ ] When YAML is valid, prints `Valid YAML: {filePath}` to stdout and exits with code 0\n    - [ ] When YAML is invalid, prints `Invalid YAML: {filePath}` followed by `Error on line {N}: {message}` (or `Error on line {N}, column {C}: {message}` if column is available) to stderr and exits with code 1\n    - [ ] File is opened read-only; no `eval()` or dynamic code execution on file content\n\n- [ ] **T3**: Create comprehensive unit tests for the YAML validation engine (`src/yaml-parser.test.ts`) `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#72-unit-tests-srcyaml-parsertestts](design.md#72-unit-tests-srcyaml-parsertestts)\n\n    **Effort**: 6 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] File `src/yaml-parser.test.ts` exists and imports `validateYaml` from `./yaml-parser`\n    - [ ] Contains valid YAML test cases that assert `{ valid: true }` for: simple key-value mapping, nested mappings, simple sequences, nested sequences, inline comments, full-line comments, empty string, whitespace-only, comment-only, single-quoted strings, double-quoted strings, literal block scalar (`|`), folded block scalar (`>`), flow mapping (`{}`), flow sequence (`[]`), document markers (`---`, `...`), multiple documents, boolean/null values, and anchors/aliases\n    - [ ] Contains invalid YAML test cases that assert `{ valid: false }` with correct `error.line` and `error.message` for: tab indentation, unterminated double quote, unterminated single quote, unclosed flow mapping, unclosed flow sequence, extra closing brace, and bad indentation (decrease to non-ancestor level)\n    - [ ] Each invalid test case verifies the `error.line` matches the expected line number\n    - [ ] Achieves at least 30 individual test cases total\n    - [ ] All tests pass when run via `bun test`\n\n### Integration\n\n- [ ] **T4**: Create CLI integration tests (`src/validate-yaml.test.ts`) using `Bun.spawn` to test the command end-to-end `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#73-integration-tests-srcvalidate-yamltestts](design.md#73-integration-tests-srcvalidate-yamltestts)\n\n    **Effort**: 4 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] File `src/validate-yaml.test.ts` exists and uses `Bun.spawn` to invoke `bun src/validate-yaml.ts` as a subprocess\n    - [ ] Tests no-argument invocation: stderr contains \"Usage:\", exit code is 1\n    - [ ] Tests valid YAML file: stdout contains \"Valid YAML:\", exit code is 0\n    - [ ] Tests invalid YAML file: stderr contains \"Invalid YAML:\" and a line number reference, exit code is 1\n    - [ ] Tests nonexistent file path: stderr contains \"File not found\", exit code is 1\n    - [ ] Tests empty YAML file: stdout contains \"Valid YAML:\", exit code is 0\n    - [ ] Tests directory path: stderr contains \"Cannot read file\" or similar, exit code is 1\n    - [ ] Uses temporary files created in test setup and cleaned up in teardown\n    - [ ] All tests pass when run via `bun test`\n\n- [ ] **T5**: Add the `validate` script entry to `package.json` `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#34-integration-packagejson](design.md#34-integration-packagejson)\n\n    **Effort**: 0.5 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] `package.json` `scripts` object contains `\"validate\": \"bun run src/validate-yaml.ts\"`\n    - [ ] Running `bun run validate` invokes the CLI entry point script\n    - [ ] No new entries are added to `dependencies` (FR-007)\n    - [ ] No existing scripts are modified or removed\n\n### User Docs\n\n- [ ] **TD1**: Update README.md - Scripts section `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#documentation-impact](design.md#documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: edit\n\n    **Target**: README.md\n\n    **Section**: Scripts\n\n    **KB Source**: -\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Scripts section includes `bun run validate <file.yaml>` with description \"Validate YAML file syntax\"\n    - [ ] Existing script entries remain unchanged\n\n- [ ] **TD2**: Update README.md - Structure section `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#documentation-impact](design.md#documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: edit\n\n    **Target**: README.md\n\n    **Section**: Structure\n\n    **KB Source**: -\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Structure diagram includes `validate-yaml.ts - YAML validation CLI command`\n    - [ ] Structure diagram includes `yaml-parser.ts   - YAML syntax validation engine`\n    - [ ] Existing structure entries remain unchanged\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Checklist\n\n- [ ] AC (FR-001-1): Running the command with a valid file path argument targets that file for validation\n- [ ] AC (FR-001-2): Running the command with no file path argument produces a usage message explaining expected input\n- [ ] AC (FR-002-1): A file containing valid YAML syntax is reported as valid\n- [ ] AC (FR-002-2): A file containing invalid YAML syntax (e.g., bad indentation, unclosed quotes, invalid characters) is reported as invalid\n- [ ] AC (FR-002-3): An empty file is handled gracefully (empty content is valid YAML per the spec)\n- [ ] AC (FR-003-1): A success message is printed that includes the file path/name\n- [ ] AC (FR-003-2): The message is concise and unambiguous (e.g., indicates the file is valid YAML)\n- [ ] AC (FR-004-1): The error message includes the file path/name\n- [ ] AC (FR-004-2): The error message includes the line number of the detected error\n- [ ] AC (FR-004-3): The error message includes a human-readable description of the syntax problem\n- [ ] AC (FR-005-1): Exit code is 0 after successful validation of a valid YAML file\n- [ ] AC (FR-005-2): Exit code is 1 after detecting invalid YAML syntax\n- [ ] AC (FR-005-3): Exit code is 1 when the specified file does not exist or cannot be read\n- [ ] AC (FR-006-1): A \"file not found\" scenario produces a clear error message indicating the file does not exist\n- [ ] AC (FR-006-2): A permissions error produces a message indicating the file cannot be read\n- [ ] AC (FR-006-3): File-level errors are distinguishable from YAML syntax errors in the output\n- [ ] AC (FR-007-1): The `dependencies` field in `package.json` has no new entries after the feature is implemented\n- [ ] AC (FR-007-2): The YAML parsing capability comes from the runtime or from code authored within the project\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] All tasks completed\n- [ ] All AC verified\n- [ ] Code reviewed\n- [ ] Docs updated\n"
