        "content": "# Technical Design: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator-command\n**Version**: 1.0.0\n**Status**: Draft\n**Created**: 2026-02-20\n\n---\n\n## 1. Design Overview\n\nThis feature adds a CLI command that validates YAML files for syntactic correctness. The command accepts one or more file paths, reads each file, parses it as YAML, and reports whether each file is well-formed. Errors include the file name, line number, and a human-readable description. The implementation uses zero new dependencies, relying on a hand-written YAML syntax validator.\n\n### High-Level Architecture\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    A[User / CI] -->|\"bun run validate-yaml file1.yml file2.yml\"| B[CLI Entry Point<br/>validate-yaml.ts]\n    B -->|reads args| C[Argument Parser]\n    B -->|reads files| D[Bun File I/O]\n    D -->|file content| E[YAML Parser Module<br/>yaml-parser.ts]\n    E -->|validation result| B\n    B -->|success to stdout<br/>errors to stderr| A\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Architecture\n\n### Component Architecture\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TB\n    subgraph CLI Layer\n        VP[validate-yaml.ts<br/>Entry Point]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Core Logic\n        YP[yaml-parser.ts<br/>YAML Syntax Validator]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Runtime\n        FS[Bun File I/O]\n        PROC[process.argv / process.exit]\n        STDIO[stdout / stderr]\n    end\n\n    VP --> YP\n    VP --> FS\n    VP --> PROC\n    VP --> STDIO\n    YP -.->|ValidationResult| VP\n```\n\n### Component Responsibilities\n\n| Component | File | Responsibility |\n|-----------|------|---------------|\n| CLI Entry Point | `src/validate-yaml.ts` | Argument parsing, file reading, output formatting, exit code management |\n| YAML Parser | `src/yaml-parser.ts` | YAML syntax validation, error detection with line numbers, multi-document support |\n\n### Sequence: Validate Multiple Files\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant CLI as validate-yaml.ts\n    participant FS as File System\n    participant Parser as yaml-parser.ts\n\n    User->>CLI: bun run validate-yaml a.yml b.yml\n    CLI->>CLI: Parse process.argv (extract file paths)\n\n    loop For each file path\n        CLI->>FS: Check file exists (Bun.file)\n        alt File not found\n            CLI->>User: stderr: \"Error: File not found: a.yml\"\n        else File exists\n            FS-->>CLI: File content (string)\n            CLI->>Parser: validateYaml(content)\n            Parser-->>CLI: ValidationResult\n            alt Valid\n                CLI->>User: stdout: \"Valid: a.yml\"\n            else Invalid\n                CLI->>User: stderr: \"Error: a.yml:3 - unexpected character\"\n            end\n        end\n    end\n\n    CLI->>CLI: process.exit(allValid ? 0 : 1)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Detailed Design\n\n### 3.1 Data Types\n\n```typescript\n/** Result of validating a single YAML document or file. */\ninterface ValidationResult {\n  valid: boolean;\n  errors: ValidationError[];\n}\n\n/** A single syntax error found during YAML validation. */\ninterface ValidationError {\n  line: number;\n  column: number;\n  message: string;\n}\n```\n\n### 3.2 YAML Parser Module (`src/yaml-parser.ts`)\n\n**Exported API:**\n\n```typescript\n/**\n * Validate a string as YAML syntax.\n * Handles multi-document YAML (--- separators).\n * Returns a ValidationResult with any syntax errors found.\n */\nexport function validateYaml(content: string): ValidationResult;\n```\n\n**Internal Design:**\n\nThe parser performs a line-by-line structural analysis of the YAML content. It is NOT a full YAML spec parser -- it is a syntax validator that detects common structural errors.\n\n**Validation checks include:**\n\n1. **Indentation consistency** -- mixed tabs and spaces, inconsistent indent levels within a mapping or sequence\n2. **Unclosed quoted strings** -- single and double quotes that span incorrectly\n3. **Invalid mapping syntax** -- missing colon after key, duplicate keys at same level\n4. **Invalid sequence syntax** -- malformed block sequence entries\n5. **Document boundary handling** -- `---` and `...` markers, validate each document independently\n6. **Flow collection matching** -- unmatched `{}`/`[]` brackets\n7. **Invalid characters** -- tabs in wrong positions, control characters\n8. **Empty file handling** -- treated as valid (per BR-02)\n\n**Multi-document strategy:**\n\nSplit content on `---` document separators (respecting that `---` must appear at the start of a line), then validate each document segment independently, tracking line offsets so reported line numbers are accurate to the original file.\n\n**Security consideration (NFR):**\n\nThe parser performs read-only structural analysis. It does not evaluate, execute, or instantiate any YAML tags, anchors that reference external resources, or custom constructors. No `!!python/exec` or similar dangerous tags are honored.\n\n### 3.3 CLI Entry Point (`src/validate-yaml.ts`)\n\n**Behavior flow:**\n\n1. Read `process.argv.slice(2)` to get file path arguments\n2. If no arguments: print usage message to stderr, exit with code 1\n3. Initialize `hasErrors = false`\n4. For each file path:\n   a. Check if file exists using `Bun.file(path).exists()`\n   b. If not found: print error to stderr, set `hasErrors = true`, continue\n   c. Read file content using `Bun.file(path).text()`\n   d. Call `validateYaml(content)`\n   e. If valid: print success to stdout (`\"Valid: {path}\"`)\n   f. If invalid: print each error to stderr (`\"Error: {path}:{line}:{column} - {message}\"`), set `hasErrors = true`\n5. Exit with code `hasErrors ? 1 : 0`\n\n**Usage message format:**\n\n```\nUsage: bun run validate-yaml <file1.yml> [file2.yml] [...]\n\nValidates YAML files for syntax correctness.\n\nArguments:\n  file1.yml    Path to a YAML file to validate (one or more required)\n```\n\n**Output format examples:**\n\n```\n# Success\nValid: config.yml\n\n# Syntax error\nError: config.yml:15:3 - unexpected mapping value (missing key)\n\n# File not found\nError: missing.yml - file not found\n\n# Multiple files, mixed results\nValid: good.yml\nError: bad.yml:7:1 - inconsistent indentation (expected 2 spaces, found 4)\nValid: also-good.yml\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Technology Stack\n\n| Concern | Choice | Rationale |\n|---------|--------|-----------|\n| Language | TypeScript (strict) | Existing project language |\n| Runtime | Bun | Existing project runtime |\n| File I/O | Bun.file() API | Native Bun API, already available |\n| YAML Parsing | Custom implementation | Zero-dependency constraint; no built-in YAML parser confirmed in existing stack |\n| Testing | bun:test | Existing test framework |\n| CLI Argument Parsing | Raw process.argv | Existing pattern in src/index.ts; no CLI framework available |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Implementation Plan\n\n| # | Component | Description | Files |\n|---|-----------|-------------|-------|\n| T1 | YAML Parser Module | Core YAML syntax validation logic with multi-document support, line-tracking error reporting | `src/yaml-parser.ts` |\n| T2 | CLI Entry Point | Argument parsing, file I/O, output formatting, exit code logic | `src/validate-yaml.ts` |\n| T3 | YAML Parser Tests | Unit tests covering valid YAML, invalid YAML (various error types), empty files, multi-document files | `src/yaml-parser.test.ts` |\n| T4 | CLI Integration Tests | Tests for CLI behavior: no args, missing files, valid files, invalid files, multiple files, exit codes | `src/validate-yaml.test.ts` |\n| T5 | Package.json Script | Add `validate-yaml` script entry pointing to `src/validate-yaml.ts` | `package.json` |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1, T5] - YAML parser module and package.json config change are independent; no shared interface\n2. [T2, T3] - CLI entry point and parser unit tests both depend on T1 parser module being defined but are independent of each other\n3. [T4] - CLI integration tests depend on both CLI entry point (T2) and parser (T1) being functional\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T2 -> T1 (Interface: CLI imports and calls `validateYaml()` from parser module)\n- T3 -> T1 (Interface: tests import and exercise `validateYaml()` from parser module)\n- T4 -> T2 (Sequential workflow: integration tests invoke the CLI entry point)\n\n**Critical Path**: T1 -> T2 -> T4\n\n---\n\n## 7. Testing Strategy\n\n### Test Value Assessment\n\n| Test Category | Value | Rationale |\n|---------------|-------|-----------|\n| YAML syntax validation correctness | HIGH - design for | Core business logic; validates that the parser correctly identifies valid/invalid YAML |\n| Error message quality (line numbers, descriptions) | HIGH - design for | Key user-facing requirement (FR-02); errors must be actionable |\n| Multi-file aggregation and exit codes | HIGH - design for | CI integration depends on correct exit codes (FR-03, STORY-04) |\n| Missing file handling | MEDIUM - design for | App-specific error handling (FR-04) |\n| Usage message display | LOW - design for | Simple output check (FR-05) |\n| Empty file acceptance | MEDIUM - design for | Business rule BR-02 edge case |\n\n### Test Plan\n\n**Unit Tests (`src/yaml-parser.test.ts`)**:\n\n| Test | Input | Expected |\n|------|-------|----------|\n| Valid simple mapping | `key: value` | `{ valid: true, errors: [] }` |\n| Valid nested mapping | indented key-value pairs | `{ valid: true, errors: [] }` |\n| Valid block sequence | `- item1\\n- item2` | `{ valid: true, errors: [] }` |\n| Valid multi-document | `---\\nfoo: 1\\n---\\nbar: 2` | `{ valid: true, errors: [] }` |\n| Valid empty content | `\"\"` | `{ valid: true, errors: [] }` |\n| Valid quoted strings | single and double quoted values | `{ valid: true, errors: [] }` |\n| Invalid: bad indentation | inconsistent spaces | `{ valid: false, errors: [{line, message}] }` |\n| Invalid: unclosed quote | `key: \"unclosed` | `{ valid: false, errors: [{line, message}] }` |\n| Invalid: tab character | tab in indentat