        "content": "# Development Tasks: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator-command\n**Status**: Not Started\n**Progress**: 0% (0 of 7 tasks)\n**Estimated Effort**: 3 days\n**Started**: 2026-02-20\n\n## Overview\n\nA CLI command that validates YAML files for syntactic correctness. The command accepts one or more file paths, parses each as YAML using a custom hand-written syntax validator (zero new dependencies), and reports whether each file is well-formed with actionable error messages including file name, line number, and description.\n\n## Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1, T5] - YAML parser module and package.json config change are independent; no shared interface\n2. [T2, T3] - CLI entry point and parser unit tests both depend on T1 parser module being defined but are independent of each other\n3. [T4] - CLI integration tests depend on both CLI entry point (T2) and parser (T1) being functional\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T2 -> T1 (Interface: CLI imports and calls `validateYaml()` from parser module)\n- T3 -> T1 (Interface: tests import and exercise `validateYaml()` from parser module)\n- T4 -> T2 (Sequential workflow: integration tests invoke the CLI entry point)\n\n**Critical Path**: T1 -> T2 -> T4\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Foundation (Parallel Group 1)\n\n- [ ] **T1**: Implement YAML Parser Module with multi-document support and line-tracking error reporting `[complexity:complex]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#32-yaml-parser-module-srcyaml-parserts](design.md#32-yaml-parser-module-srcyaml-parserts)\n\n    **Effort**: 8 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] File `src/yaml-parser.ts` exists and exports `validateYaml(content: string): ValidationResult`\n    - [ ] `ValidationResult` interface has `valid: boolean` and `errors: ValidationError[]`\n    - [ ] `ValidationError` interface has `line: number`, `column: number`, and `message: string`\n    - [ ] Detects indentation consistency errors (mixed tabs/spaces, inconsistent indent levels)\n    - [ ] Detects unclosed quoted strings (single and double quotes)\n    - [ ] Detects invalid mapping syntax (missing colon after key, duplicate keys at same level)\n    - [ ] Detects invalid sequence syntax (malformed block sequence entries)\n    - [ ] Handles document boundaries (`---` and `...` markers), validates each document independently\n    - [ ] Detects unmatched flow collection brackets (`{}`, `[]`)\n    - [ ] Detects invalid characters (tabs in wrong positions, control characters)\n    - [ ] Empty string input returns `{ valid: true, errors: [] }`\n    - [ ] Multi-document files report line numbers relative to the original file, not per-document offsets\n    - [ ] Parser performs read-only structural analysis only; does not evaluate or execute YAML tags or constructors\n    - [ ] No new dependencies added to `package.json`\n\n- [ ] **T5**: Add `validate-yaml` script entry to package.json `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#5-implementation-plan](design.md#5-implementation-plan)\n\n    **Effort**: 1 hour\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] `package.json` contains a `scripts` entry for `validate-yaml` pointing to `src/validate-yaml.ts`\n    - [ ] Running `bun run validate-yaml` invokes the CLI entry point\n    - [ ] No new entries added to `dependencies` or `devDependencies`\n\n### Core Logic and Unit Tests (Parallel Group 2)\n\n- [ ] **T2**: Implement CLI Entry Point with argument parsing, file I/O, and output formatting `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#33-cli-entry-point-srcvalidate-yamlts](design.md#33-cli-entry-point-srcvalidate-yamlts)\n\n    **Effort**: 2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] File `src/validate-yaml.ts` exists and is executable via `bun src/validate-yaml.ts`\n    - [ ] Reads file paths from `process.argv.slice(2)`\n    - [ ] With no arguments: prints usage message to stderr and exits with code 1\n    - [ ] For each file: checks existence via `Bun.file(path).exists()`, reads content via `Bun.file(path).text()`\n    - [ ] Missing file: prints `\"Error: {path} - file not found\"` to stderr and sets non-zero exit\n    - [ ] Valid file: prints `\"Valid: {path}\"` to stdout\n    - [ ] Invalid file: prints `\"Error: {path}:{line}:{column} - {message}\"` to stderr for each error\n    - [ ] Exits with code 0 if all files valid, code 1 if any file invalid or missing\n    - [ ] Imports `validateYaml` from `./yaml-parser`\n\n- [ ] **T3**: Write YAML Parser unit tests covering valid, invalid, empty, and multi-document YAML `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#7-testing-strategy](design.md#7-testing-strategy)\n\n    **Effort**: 5 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] File `src/yaml-parser.test.ts` exists and all tests pass via `bun test`\n    - [ ] Tests valid simple mapping (`key: value`) returns `{ valid: true, errors: [] }`\n    - [ ] Tests valid nested mapping returns valid result\n    - [ ] Tests valid block sequence (`- item1\\n- item2`) returns valid result\n    - [ ] Tests valid multi-document (`---\\nfoo: 1\\n---\\nbar: 2`) returns valid result\n    - [ ] Tests empty content returns `{ valid: true, errors: [] }`\n    - [ ] Tests valid quoted strings (single and double) return valid result\n    - [ ] Tests invalid indentation returns `{ valid: false }` with error including line number\n    - [ ] Tests unclosed quote returns error with line number\n    - [ ] Tests tab character in indentation returns error with line number\n    - [ ] Tests unmatched bracket (`[a, b`) returns error with line number\n    - [ ] Tests duplicate key at same level returns error with line number\n    - [ ] Tests multi-document with one bad document returns error with correct line number from original file\n    - [ ] All error results include `line > 0` and a descriptive `message`\n\n### Integration Testing (Parallel Group 3)\n\n- [ ] **T4**: Write CLI integration tests covering no-args, missing files, valid files, invalid files, multiple files, and exit codes `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#7-testing-strategy](design.md#7-testing-strategy)\n\n    **Effort**: 5 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] File `src/validate-yaml.test.ts` exists and all tests pass via `bun test`\n    - [ ] Tests no-arguments scenario: usage message on stderr, exit code 1\n    - [ ] Tests valid file scenario: success message on stdout containing file path, exit code 0\n    - [ ] Tests invalid file scenario: error on stderr with line info, exit code 1\n    - [ ] Tests missing file scenario: \"file not found\" message on stderr, exit code 1\n    - [ ] Tests multiple valid files: success for each on stdout, exit code 0\n    - [ ] Tests mixed valid/invalid files: success for valid on stdout, error for invalid on stderr, exit code 1\n    - [ ] Tests empty file: treated as valid, success on stdout, exit code 0\n    - [ ] Tests use temporary files created and cleaned up within each test\n    - [ ] Tests invoke CLI via `Bun.spawn` or equivalent to verify actual process behavior\n\n### User Docs\n\n- [ ] **TD1**: Update README.md - Scripts `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#documentation-impact](design.md#documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: edit\n\n    **Target**: README.md\n\n    **Section**: Scripts\n\n    **KB Source**: -\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] README.md Scripts section includes the `validate-yaml` command with usage description\n    - [ ] Command syntax and example invocation are documented\n\n- [ ] **TD2**: Update README.md - Structure `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#documentation-impact](design.md#documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: edit\n\n    **Target**: README.md\n\n    **Section**: Structure\n\n    **KB Source**: -\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] README.md Structure section includes `src/yaml-parser.ts` and `src/validate-yaml.ts`\n    - [ ] New test files `src/yaml-parser.test.ts` and `src/validate-yaml.test.ts` are listed if test files are part of structure diagram\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Checklist\n\n- [ ] FR-01: Single file validation -- valid YAML returns success + exit 0; invalid YAML returns error + non-zero exit\n- [ ] FR-02: Error reporting includes file name, line number, and descriptive message\n- [ ] FR-03: Multiple file validation -- individual results for each file; exit 0 only if all valid\n- [ ] FR-04: Missing file produces clear \"file not found\" error, non-zero exit, no stack trace\n- [ ] FR-05: No-argument invocation displays usage message, non-zero exit\n- [ ] FR-06: No new entries in `dependencies` or `devDependencies` in `package.json`\n- [ ] BR-01: Validates syntax only, not schema or semantic correctness\n- [ ] BR-02: Empty files treated as valid YAML\n- [ ] BR-03: Multi-document files (`---` separated) have each document validated; file invalid if any document has errors\n- [ ] BR-04: No new packages added to `package.json`\n- [ ] NFR: Validation of a file under 10,000 lines completes in under 2 seconds\n- [ ] NFR: Errors to stderr, success to stdout\n- [ ] NFR: Parser does not evaluate or execute any YAML tags or constructors\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] All tasks completed\n- [ ] All AC verified\n- [ ] Code reviewed\n- [ ] Docs updated\n"
